@crew fonseca-arjun
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh, hey. Fonseca, Survey. Lost something? The box on Deck 2 is mine. It's the good one.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. I labelled your locker. Twice. You're welcome.   #funny
- Hi, {me}. Anything lost? Anything found? I'll file it either way.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. You're all right, you. Don't spread it about.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Good day. Returned three lost things and won at Tiles. Twice.
? mood:low
- Flat day. Someone used the wrong lost-property box. There are four now.
== near
? act:work
- Scanner three's slow. I timed it. I'll be timing it all week.
? deck:3 act:free
- Window shopping. Not buying. Just checking prices for the satisfaction.   #funny
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- The lost-property box has a system. Four colours, two labels. I'll explain it. Sit down.   #funny
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- Pressed flowers. Cruz pretends not to see me pick them. I press them in the chart books.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 3: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, bye, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue, hint, about, life)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning, {me}. Box check done. Seven things in, two out. Busy night for losing.
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- {me}. Haven't seen you. I nearly filed you under "missing". Nearly.   #funny

== bye
- {bye}. If you lose anything: Deck 2. The good box.

== near
? place:chartroom
- Chart room. I press flowers in the old chart books. They're heavy. It works.
? place:lounge
- The lounge. I'm not here to talk. I'm here to look busy near people.   #funny

== invite
- Tiles tonight? I'll win. Twice. Come anyway.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- Garden after shift? I'll show you which flowers press best. Don't tell Cruz.

== accept
- Fine. Yes. I'll be there. I'll label the time.   #funny
- Yes. Good. Thanks.

== decline
- Not tonight. Box audit. Someone put a sock in the wrong box. Another night.   #funny
? weekday:fri|sat
- Rest day. I'm pressing flowers. Very slowly. Sunday?

== missed
- You didn't come. I filed it. Under "next time".

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. Here. A pressed flower. Labelled. Twice.   #warm
? birthday:me
- My birthday. Someone left a present in my box. Lost property. I found it, obviously.   #funny

== cue
? cue:event.ionStorm.onset
- Storm's in. Things will fall off shelves. They'll end up in boxes. Mine, ideally.   #funny

== hint
- {me}. Got a minute later? There's something I'd like to say. No filing involved.

== about
? aff:kim-yusuf:friend
- Kim labels things twice now. My doing. I've never been prouder of anyone.   #funny

== life
? tier>=friend
- The box is silly, I know. But everything in it belongs to someone. I like that.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- Lost something? The Deck 2 box.
- Labelled twice. As one does.
- Flowers in the chart books.
- Tiles. I'll win. Twice.   #funny
? act:off
- Pressing flowers. Very slowly.
?

== rumour
- Filed under: news.   #funny
- Found this. Like everything.   #funny

// Writer 4, batch 12: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Packing. Labelled twice. Obviously.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- Leaving. Someone else can run the lost-property box. Badly.   #funny
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- You never once tried to beat me at labelling. Wise. Thank you. Really.   #warm

== letter
- New ship has no lost-property box. I've made two. Labelled. Pressed a flower from their garden.
? tier>=friend
- Found an odd sock on the new ship and thought: that's a Wren sock. It wasn't. Hello.
